{"type":"standard","title":"Bedik language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Bedik language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q35096","titles":{"canonical":"Bedik_language","normalized":"Bedik language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Bedik language</span></span>"},"pageid":33151692,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1312339385","tid":"6b086909-95ce-11f0-9e3e-e13cb7264f42","timestamp":"2025-09-20T03:03:44Z","description":"Senegambian language spoken in Senegal","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedik_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedik_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedik_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Bedik_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedik_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Bedik_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedik_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Bedik_language"}},"extract":"Bedik, also Banda, is a Senegambian language of Senegal and Guinea spoken by traditional hunter-gatherers. Other names include Bande, Basari du Bandemba, Bedik, Budik, Manik, Münik, Onik, Tandanke, Tenda, Tendanke.","extract_html":"<p><b>Bedik</b>, also <i>Banda</i>, is a Senegambian language of Senegal and Guinea spoken by traditional hunter-gatherers. Other names include Bande, Basari du Bandemba, Bedik, Budik, Manik, Münik, Onik, Tandanke, Tenda, Tendanke.</p>"}